THE FINDING THAT DECIDED THE BUILD

Both briefs specify public/ URLs: `/images/sliders/<id>-after.webp` and
`/proof/<file>.webp`. Those are 404s on this host.

audit/FINDINGS.md F-131 measured it: `/qr-app.jpg`, from the REPO-ROOT public/,
returns 200; `/icon-192.png`, which has sat in apps/web/public since long before
any of this work, returns 404 — and so did all 28 illustrations written there.
data/floor-images.ts, data/machine-images.ts and data/illustration-images.ts all
carry the same workaround in their first line. 108 photographs and 135 diagrams
render on the live site precisely because they are imported rather than served.

So the naive read of the brief unzips cleanly, commits 58 correct files, passes
every source-reading guard, and shows 36 broken-image icons in production. That
is F-131 verbatim, for the third time. app/data/slider-images.ts statically
imports all 58 frames; the registry holds keys into it and cannot hold a URL.

FOUR ARCHIVES, MEASURED RATHER THAN COMPARED BY EYE

  slider packs   16 pairs, every frame 1920x1280, exactly 3:2, locked camera
  proof packs    13 plates at 1168x784, one pair PORTRAIT (784x1168), and one
                 whose two frames were DIFFERENT SIZES — screen-recoat shipped
                 a 1712x1152 before against a 1168x784 after, while declaring
                 itself `status: 'slider-ready'`

A comparison handle cannot track across two pixel grids, so that was a
functional defect, not a preference. Five proof plates also carried
`status: 'recapture'` — the camera drifted between frames. The slider pairs have
neither problem.

So: the IMAGES come from the slider packs, the WORDS come from the proof packs.
Nothing was rewritten to fit. headline, factline, both alts, the route lists and
the CTAs are the supplied copy, parsed out of proof-plates.ts and
proof-plates-batch-02.ts rather than retyped.

Three plates stay on their proof frames because only that pack has them:
`problems-cupping`, `screen-recoat`, and `dust-free-occupied` — which keeps its
DURING frame deliberately, since containment-up is the entire point of that
placement and no slider pair has it. screen-recoat's before frame was resampled
1712x1152 → 1168x784 (same aspect to three decimals, so a resize and not a crop).

Five slider pairs had no proof plate — 11, 12, 14, 15, 16 — and get headlines
built from the site's own documented formula, "Same [x]. Same [y]. Different
floor.", with alts that describe what is in the frame. No price, no moisture
reading, no day count, no name.

18 plates, one registry at content/proof-sliders.ts. Batch 02 merged in and both
source files deleted, as briefed.

TWO ROUTES REMOVED, AND IT IS A DECISION NOT A DETAIL

The supplied registry put `herringboneCondo` and `customInlay` on /design and
/library. Two of the three briefs forbid exactly those pages — "DO NOT put
sliders on /papers /glossary /data /framework /library /design", and again
"those pages win as engineering. A beauty slider there cheapens the corpus."
The third asked for them. The prohibition is stated twice and reasoned once, so
it wins; the guard enforces it and the registry records why. Reversing it is one
line per entry plus a change to FORBIDDEN, which is the right amount of friction.

THE COMPONENT

ProofSlider. Not IllustrationPair — a cross-fade destroys the one thing that
makes a before/after persuasive, which is that the chair and the window do not
move while the floor changes.

The control is a native <input type="range">, styled to look like a handle
rather than replaced by one. That is the entire accessibility story: mouse drag,
touch drag, arrow keys, Home/End, PageUp/PageDown, a role, a value and a label —
all of it already correct, none of it reimplemented. The usual build is a div
with pointer handlers, and it is how comparison sliders end up keyboard-dead.

The AFTER frame is CLIPPED, never hidden. Both images stay in the DOM with both
alts, so a crawler or a reader-mode parser that cannot drag still receives what
changed, alongside the headline and factline as ordinary prose.

There is no autoplay to disable, so prefers-reduced-motion removes the easing on
the wipe and nothing else — the control keeps working.

MOUNTED: the homepage only, above the JobCardRail. That is the conversion test
both briefs name, and P1/P2 is mounting, not building.

imageSlot IS STILL EMPTY. Both briefs asked me to fill it with the AFTER stills.
job-cards.ts says it is "Reserved for real job photography. Left undefined on
purpose", and the brief's own precedence rule says that file wins. A generated
floor beside a real MVTR reading is the exact thing that comment exists to
prevent. The guard fails the build if anyone points it at a slider frame.

scripts/verify-sliders.mjs — five checks, four of which exist because the
delivered archives already contained the defect: every frame statically imported
(F-131), every pair the same size (screen-recoat), no invented case study (pair
01 is the homepage slider and has no published job), routes real and permitted,
and nothing claiming to be a photograph.

50 guards green. tsc at the 107-error Prisma sandbox baseline, none in new code.

